Open Vanilla 0059: the bots fight Onyxia (realm/bossfights/onyxia-strategy.md). The playerbots' Onyxia strategy was an
empty stub; now, in Onyxia's Lair, with the dungeon strategies on (Boss Fights' fill bots have them):
  phases 1 and 3: her target holds her at the north wall facing it (tank spot 6, -214.5); every other bot stays at
    her sides, out of her front cone (Flame Breath, Cleave, Wing Buffet: ±60°, 40 yd) and her tail cone (Tail Sweep:
    ±60°, 30 yd): melee at her flank, ranged and healers 22 yd out;
  phase 2 (in the air, 65-40%): every bot keeps out of the Deep Breath line (from her spot through the middle of the
    room, 9 yd either side) by moving square to it, 17 yd off, inside the floor and away from the egg tunnels; checked
    every second and as a reaction;
  phase 3: a shaman keeps a Tremor Totem down; a priest with Fear Ward keeps it on her tank.
Pure geometry in playerbot/strategy/generic/OnyxiaGeometry.h (tested by realm/bossfights/tests/test_onyxia.cpp).

Boss Fights: OpenVanilla.BossFights.BotRaid.Health / .Damage (default 1.0: no change) soften a raid that is at least
.BotRaid.Share (0.5) bots at tier .BotRaid.MaxTier (1) or below - the owner's call. The real-fight self-test's test
commands (self-test accounts only): "test pull" (the account a spectator - game master - in a corner, the run's bots
around Onyxia, Onyxia on the bot tank), "test boss" (tboss,<alive>,<health %>,<phase>,<in combat>), "test spectate
on|off"; "test reset" ends a spectator.

